# Direct dependencies of the backend image (see Dockerfile) and of the
# local development environment. Hash-Lock folgt spaeter -- requirements.txt
# is currently a plain `pip freeze` of the resolved tree, not a
# `pip-compile --generate-hashes` lock (see requirements.txt's own header),
# same as Weave-Retrieval's/Weave-Knowledge's backend/requirements.in.
#
# fastapi/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pytest/httpx/PyYAML pins are kept
# identical to Weave-Retrieval's backend/requirements.in -- no reason for
# these to drift between sibling services without cause. Deliberately NO
# sqlalchemy/alembic/celery/redis here: Weave-Runtime is the stateless
# bot-orchestrator (see README's "Nicht-Ziele") -- it owns no schema to
# migrate and no task queue to run, only synchronous HTTP calls out to
# Weave-Retrieval or an LLM provider (httpx) and YAML bot configs (PyYAML, see
# app/services/botconfig.py).
